  "label": "The act of applying nail polish is mapped onto Hitler's vanity",
  "description": "The visual scene of applying nail polish (person_applying_nail_polish) is mapped onto the textual implication that Hitler 'has to show them off'. The text 'you never know when you have to show them off' is projected onto the visual act of nail application, which is then associated with Hitler. This mapping suggests that Hitler's vanity is analogous to the act of beautifying one's nails.",
